[344.782041, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m[MOTU]\u001b[0m Alright, let’s talk about this Build-Depends list – it’s a crucial part of your Debian/Ubuntu packaging! During the build process, `Build-Depends` specifies *essential* runtime dependencies – packages that absolutely *must* be installed alongside your software for it to function correctly. As you’re reviewing it, you should meticulously check that every listed package is truly required and that the versions specified are compatible with your software (refer to Debian Policy Manual section 8.3.2 for versioning considerations). A common pitfall is including packages solely because they're *used* by your software, rather than truly *needed* at runtime – avoid this and only list dependencies directly required for execution. Finally, remember to review the list carefully, as incorrect dependencies can lead to frustrating runtime errors for your users!\r\n"]
[344.782189, "o", "\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mWrite Build-Depends to debian/control? [y/N]:\u001b[0m "]
[403.961288, "o", "y"]
[404.726483, "o", "\r\n"]
