[690.163319, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m[MOTU]\u001b[0m Okay, let’s break down this Build-Depends list generated by the Detect agent. Essentially, this list outlines all the packages required *during the build process* of your software – these are the dependencies your software needs to compile and create its executable. As per the Debian Policy Manual, Section 7.6.1 (\"Build Dependencies\"), these packages are crucial for ensuring your software can successfully transform source code into a usable application.  Specifically, you should verify each entry to ensure it’s truly necessary, and that the listed packages are providing the correct runtime and build-time support (e.g., compilers, libraries, development headers).  Your next packaging step should be to *explicitly* include these Build-Depends in your package’s `debian/control` (or equivalent) file, ensuring they’re correctly listed under the `Build-Depends` field – this ensures they’re installed alongside your software during the packaging process.\r\n\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRun another skill? [Y/n]:\u001b[0m "]
